      "title": "https://www.unknowncheats.me/forum/general-programming-and-reversing/777280-scylla-dumper-instead-pe-sieve-reversing-post4834496.html",
      "via": "browser_llm",
      "collect_mode": "browser_llm",
      "content": "Hey everyone,\nI've noticed that across almost every tutorial and thread regarding dumping packed/protected binaries for static analysis (IDA / Ghidra), people consistently recommend using Scylla (usually via x64dbg).\nAt the same time, tools like PE-sieve exist, which can dump and automatically unmap the PE (/dmode 2) without even attaching a debugger or having to deal with basic anti-debugging checks.\nIs the widespread use of Scylla mainly just tradition/habit because most older stickied guides were written around it, or does Scylla actually have distinct technical advantages over PE-sieve when it comes to:\nResolving and rebuilding heavily obfuscated or redirected Import Address Tables (IAT)?\nHandling specific packers/protectors (e.g., custom stubs, manual entry point alignment)?\nPrecision control over search/IAT recreation ranges compared to automated heuristics?\nWould love to hear your experiences on which workflow produces cleaner, more reliable dumps for IDA in practice.\nThanks!",
      "content_format": "text/plain",
      "content_status": "ok",
      "content_via": "browser",
      "content_source_url": "https://www.unknowncheats.me/forum/general-programming-and-reversing/777280-scylla-dumper-instead-pe-sieve-reversing.html#post4834496",
